# Issues Faced During Project Execution

## 1. Virtual Machine Networking Issues

### Problem

Initially, communication between virtual machines was not working correctly. The Kali Linux machine was unable to reach the Windows machine and the SIEM server.

### Root Cause

Incorrect VirtualBox network adapter configuration.

### Resolution

* Verified VirtualBox network settings.
* Configured all virtual machines to use Host-Only Adapter.
* Assigned valid IP addresses.
* Tested connectivity using ping.

### Lesson Learned

Always verify network communication before installing monitoring tools.

---

## 2. Wazuh Agent Registration Issues

### Problem

The Kali Linux agent was not appearing in the Wazuh dashboard.

### Root Cause

Incorrect Wazuh Manager IP address and agent service issues.

### Resolution

* Verified manager IP configuration.
* Restarted Wazuh agent service.
* Checked agent status using systemctl.

### Lesson Learned

Agent communication should be verified immediately after installation.

---

## 3. Wazuh Dashboard Access Warning

### Problem

Browser displayed SSL certificate warnings when accessing the Wazuh dashboard.

### Root Cause

Wazuh uses self-signed certificates by default.

### Resolution

* Accepted the certificate warning.
* Continued access through HTTPS.

### Lesson Learned

Self-signed certificates are common in lab environments but should be replaced in production environments.

---

## 4. Sysmon Log Visibility Issues

### Problem

Sysmon logs were not visible inside Wazuh after installation.

### Root Cause

Sysmon event channel was not configured in ossec.conf.

### Resolution

Added:

```xml
<localfile>
  <location>Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational</location>
  <log_format>eventchannel</log_format>
</localfile>
```

Restarted the Wazuh agent.

### Lesson Learned

Proper log forwarding configuration is required for centralized monitoring.

---

## 5. OpenVAS Scan Delays

### Problem

Vulnerability scans required significant time to complete.

### Root Cause

Limited virtual machine resources and comprehensive scan profile.

### Resolution

* Allowed scans to complete without interruption.
* Allocated additional RAM where possible.

### Lesson Learned

Vulnerability scans can be resource intensive and require planning.

---

## 6. Resource Constraints

### Problem

Running multiple virtual machines simultaneously increased CPU and RAM usage.

### Resolution

* Closed unnecessary applications.
* Optimized VM resource allocation.

### Lesson Learned

Proper hardware planning is important when building cybersecurity labs.

---

# Summary

Despite multiple technical challenges, all issues were successfully resolved through troubleshooting, log analysis, and configuration adjustments. The experience improved practical understanding of deployment, monitoring, and infrastructure management.
